  "result": "All 5 tests pass.\n\n**Result**\n\n```\n5 passed in 0.07s\n```\n\nI chose Approach B, SQLite, in `kvstore/store.py`. The store creates one `kv` table with a primary-keyed `key` column and commits each write immediately, so it is transactional and persists across instances without loading the whole file. I kept the default rollback-journal mode rather than WAL because WAL would leave `-wal` and `-shm` side files next to the database, which the spec's single-file rule and the last test forbid.\n\nThe `Store` also supports use as a context manager and raises a clear error if used after `close()`. I did not commit the change since you didn't ask for one.",
